Expose reading_form and dictionary_form on the WASM Morpheme binding,
and disable wasm-opt.

The upstream binding only exports surface / part_of_speech / normalized_form.
Kotonoha needs the per-token reading (katakana, from UniDic) to
disambiguate kana homographs (家の前 まえ vs ぜん, 頭 read かしら → head/leader)
and to display accurate furigana, and the dictionary form as a
better conjugation base. wasm-opt is disabled because it downloads binaryen
from GitHub at build time (blocked in proxied environments) and the
unoptimized binary performs fine for this workload.

Applied by scripts/setup-sudachi.sh after checking out the pinned commit of
https://github.com/hi-ogawa/sudachi.rs — regenerate with `git diff` in the
clone if the pin is ever bumped.

